-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Reference models and standards
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The simulation implements published, non-proprietary models. They are recorded
here as provenance, not as licensed material: no code was copied from any
reference implementation, and each model is implemented independently from its
published description.

Standards, both public-domain U.S. Government publications:

  * U.S. Standard Atmosphere, 1976 -- the seven standard lapse-rate layers to
    86 km (sim/environment/atmosphere.py). Above 86 km the model continues with
    a piecewise-exponential thermosphere approximation, which is this project's
    own extension and not part of the 1976 standard.
  * WGS 84 geodetic datum, per NIMA TR8350.2 -- reference ellipsoid and the
    J2 through J6 zonal harmonics (sim/environment/gravity.py).

Textbook derivations consulted for the astrodynamics formulations, cited in the
relevant module docstrings:

  * Vallado, "Fundamentals of Astrodynamics and Applications", 4th ed.
  * Montenbruck and Gill, "Satellite Orbits", 3rd ed.

These are copyrighted works. Nothing from them is reproduced here; they are
listed so a reader can check the derivations against their source.

